     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Raju listed numbers from 1 to 30 and crossed out those with more than two factors.\n\"What is left?\" asked the teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "prime",
     "composite",
     "sieve"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A prime number has exactly two factors, 1 and itself. 2, 3, 5, 7, 11 and 13 are prime. A composite number has more than two factors. 1 is neither prime nor composite.\nThe sieve of Eratosthenes finds primes: cross out 1, keep 2 and cross out its multiples, keep 3 and cross out its multiples, and so on.\n2 is the only even prime."
    }
   },
